@page "/introduction"

<PageTitle>Introduction - Quark Suite</PageTitle>

<Div data-slot="docs"
     Display="Display.Flex"
     ItemsAlign="Items.Stretch"
     ScrollMargin="ScrollMargin.Is24.FromTop"
     Width="Width.IsFull"
     Padding="Padding.Is8.FromBottom"
     class="text-[1.05rem] sm:text-[15px]">
    <Div Flex="Flex.Is1" FlexDirection="FlexDirection.Col" MinWidth="MinWidth.Is0">
        <Div Height='Height.Token("h-(--top-spacing)")' Shrink="Shrink.Is0"></Div>

        <Div Margin="Margin.Auto.OnX"
             Width="Width.IsFull"
             MinWidth="MinWidth.Is0"
             Flex=@("flex flex-1 flex-col")
             Gap='Gap.Token("6")'
             class="w-full max-w-none px-0 py-6 text-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-300 sm:max-w-[40rem] lg:py-8">
            <Div Flex=@("flex flex-col") Gap="Gap.Is2">
                <H1 ScrollMargin="ScrollMargin.Is24.FromTop"
                    TextSize="TextSize.ThreeXl"
                    FontWeight="FontWeight.Semibold"
                    Tracking="Tracking.Tight"
                    TextAlign="TextAlign.Start">
                    Introduction
                </H1>

                <Paragraph TextColor="TextColor.MutedForeground"
                           TextSize="TextSize.Xl.OnSm.Base"
                           class="text-[1.05rem] sm:text-balance md:max-w-[85%]">
                    Quark Suite is a set of accessible, composable Blazor components inspired by shadcn/ui.
                </Paragraph>
            </Div>

            <Div Space="Space.Y.Is8" Width="Width.IsFull" class="*:data-[slot=alert]:first:mt-0">
                <Section Space="Space.Y.Is4">
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        It provides the building blocks for application interfaces: buttons, forms, dialogs, tables, navigation, feedback, layout, and typography. Components have useful defaults, share a consistent API, and render ordinary HTML wherever possible.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        Use the component API for routine work. When a design needs something more specific, use typed Tailwind properties, add utility classes, pass HTML and ARIA attributes, or compose the lower-level primitives directly.
                    </Paragraph>
                </Section>

                <Section Space="Space.Y.Is4">
                    <H2 TextSize="TextSize.Xl" FontWeight="FontWeight.Semibold" TextAlign="TextAlign.Start">A small example</H2>
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        Quark components are used directly in Razor. Variants and sizes are typed, while standard attributes and event handlers remain available.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <CodeEditor Text="@ButtonExample" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
                </Section>

                <Section Space="Space.Y.Is4">
                    <H2 TextSize="TextSize.Xl" FontWeight="FontWeight.Semibold" TextAlign="TextAlign.Start">What Quark provides</H2>
                    <UnorderedList Class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2">
                        <UnorderedListItem><Strong>Components:</Strong> finished interface elements with consistent behavior and shadcn-style defaults.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Strong>Primitives:</Strong> semantic building blocks for layouts and custom component composition.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Strong>Typed styling:</Strong> C# builders for common Tailwind utilities, responsive values, and theme tokens.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Strong>Escape hatches:</Strong> raw classes, styles, data attributes, ARIA attributes, and standard Razor content.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Strong>Build tooling:</Strong> generators for the Tailwind stylesheet, Lucide icon map, and optional theme CSS.</UnorderedListItem>
                    </UnorderedList>
                </Section>

                <Section Space="Space.Y.Is4">
                    <H2 TextSize="TextSize.Xl" FontWeight="FontWeight.Semibold" TextAlign="TextAlign.Start">How styling works</H2>
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        Quark uses Tailwind utilities and shadcn-compatible CSS variables. Component variants provide the default visual treatment. Shared properties such as <Code>Padding</Code>, <Code>Gap</Code>, <Code>TextColor</Code>, and <Code>Rounded</Code> emit utility classes and support responsive builder values.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <CodeEditor Text="@StylingExample" Language="razor" ReadOnly="true" AutoHeight="true" Minimap="false" ShowCopyButton="true" />
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        The <Code>Class</Code> parameter is always available for one-off utilities, state selectors, or exact overrides. Typed properties are a convenience, not a boundary.
                    </Paragraph>
                </Section>

                <Section Space="Space.Y.Is4">
                    <H2 TextSize="TextSize.Xl" FontWeight="FontWeight.Semibold" TextAlign="TextAlign.Start">How it relates to shadcn/ui</H2>
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        <Anchor Href="https://ui.shadcn.com/" Target="Target.Blank" FontWeight="FontWeight.Medium" DecorationLine="DecorationLine.Underline" LinkOffset="LinkOffset.Is4">shadcn/ui</Anchor> is the design reference for many Quark components. Naming, variants, composition, theme tokens, and visual behavior should feel familiar.
                    </Paragraph>
                    <Paragraph Leading="Leading.Relaxed">
                        The delivery model is different. shadcn/ui copies component source into an application; Quark is installed as a NuGet component library. Quark follows the same design language while favoring Razor composition, .NET types, and Blazor conventions over direct React equivalents.
                    </Paragraph>
                </Section>

                <Section Space="Space.Y.Is4">
                    <H2 TextSize="TextSize.Xl" FontWeight="FontWeight.Semibold" TextAlign="TextAlign.Start">Where to go next</H2>
                    <UnorderedList Class="list-inside list-disc space-y-2">
                        <UnorderedListItem><Anchor Href="installation" FontWeight="FontWeight.Medium" DecorationLine="DecorationLine.Underline" LinkOffset="LinkOffset.Is4">Installation</Anchor> — add the packages, generators, services, and stylesheet.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Anchor Href="components" FontWeight="FontWeight.Medium" DecorationLine="DecorationLine.Underline" LinkOffset="LinkOffset.Is4">Components</Anchor> — browse the available UI and see each API in context.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Anchor Href="properties" FontWeight="FontWeight.Medium" DecorationLine="DecorationLine.Underline" LinkOffset="LinkOffset.Is4">Properties</Anchor> — learn the typed Tailwind builder model and escape hatches.</UnorderedListItem>
                        <UnorderedListItem><Anchor Href="themes" FontWeight="FontWeight.Medium" DecorationLine="DecorationLine.Underline" LinkOffset="LinkOffset.Is4">Themes</Anchor> — configure the CSS variables used across the suite.</UnorderedListItem>
                    </UnorderedList>
                </Section>
            </Div>
        </Div>
    </Div>
</Div>

@code {
    private const string ButtonExample =
@"<Button Variant=""ButtonVariant.Outline""
        ButtonSize=""ButtonSize.Sm""
        @onclick=""Save"">
    Save changes
</Button>";

    private const string StylingExample =
@"<Div Display=""Display.Flex""
     Gap=""Gap.Is3""
     Padding=""Padding.Is4.OnMd.Is6""
     Rounded=""Rounded.Lg""
     Class=""border bg-card text-card-foreground"">
    ...
</Div>";
}
